# EI-CF + ROBOT training-data generation

The method fits Gaussian-process surrogates for intermediate measurable
properties `h(x)`, evaluates the composite detection score `g(h)`, and selects
new simulator inputs using EI-CF inside ROBOT h-space trust regions. The ROBOT
diversity constraint uses scaled L1 distance, with the threshold `tau` set by the empirical CDF of pairwise distances among measurable training events.


## Entry point

Use `run_multi_seed.py` for experiments. The `run_bo.py` module is kept only
because `run_multi_seed.py` imports its internal `run_single()` function.

## Multi-seed run

```bash
python run_multi_seed.py \
  --seeds 1-10 \
  --n-iterations 30 \
  --acquisition ROBOT_EICF \
  --robot-distance-mode tail_l1 \
  --robot-tau-quantile 75 \
  --candidate-samples 1500 \
  --eicf-mc-samples 16
```
